  <prompt>Add a `Preference` member to `Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryFactType.cs` (currently 4 members: Party/KeyDate/PriorAnalysis/KeyFact — NO Preference) and extend the `Handlers/MemoryWriteHandler.cs` wire map (~:97–104, which maps party|keyDate|priorAnalysis|keyFact) to map the new preference fact type. Ensure a preference memory item written at User scope is recalled into `userFragment` each turn via the existing recall path (`ContextBinder.ResolveUserMemoryFragmentAsync` → `ToUserPromptFragmentAsync`). Bind any CRUD-side consumer to the `PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs` v1 contract; keep `trustLevel` carried inert (ADR-042 deferred hard-governance stays deferred to security project #616). R4 owns these `Services/Ai/Memory` changes directly (redesign-r2 is closed) — no cross-team gating.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. .NET 8 Minimal API + AI memory-governance expertise; comfortable with the ADR-042 two-scope memory model, the ADR-013 AI facade boundary (PublicContracts), and the User-scope Cosmos `memory-items` store partitioned by /subjectId.</role>
  <goal>A `Preference` memory item can be written (User scope) and is recalled into `userFragment` each turn — giving standing directives a governed preference channel instead of landing as a generic `KeyFact`.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-07 — the first E3 step. `MemoryFactType.cs` (~:12–33) has exactly 4 members (Party/KeyDate/PriorAnalysis/KeyFact) — there is NO Preference type today, so standing directives land as generic `KeyFact` with no governed preference channel and FR-09's producer has nothing to gate. `MemoryWriteHandler.cs` (~:97–104) wires party|keyDate|priorAnalysis|keyFact into the write path; `IMemoryItemStore`/`MemoryItemStore` persist User-scope items to Cosmos `memory-items` partitioned by /subjectId. Recall assembles the userFragment in `ContextBinder.ResolveUserFragmentAsync` (~:553–583) = stated-profile + org + user-memory, reaching user memory via `ResolveUserMemoryFragmentAsync` (~:644) → `ToUserPromptFragmentAsync`. This task adds `Preference` + its wire map and confirms recall includes it. E3 memory work is owned entirely in R4 (redesign-r2 closed); still bind CRUD-side consumers to `PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs` v1 (MemoryScope/MemoryOrigin) and hold ADR-042's deferred hard-governance (untrusted-origin ban, trustLevel enforcement, memory-poisoning evals) deferred to #616 with `trustLevel` carried inert.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryFactType.cs (~:12–33, add `Preference` — 4 members today, no Preference)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/MemoryWriteHandler.cs (~:97–104, wire map party|keyDate|priorAnalysis|keyFact)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Memory/ (IMemoryItemStore / MemoryItemStore — User scope, Cosmos `memory-items` partitioned by /subjectId)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/ContextBinder.cs (ResolveUserFragmentAsync ~:553–583; ResolveUserMemoryFragmentAsync ~:644 → ToUserPromptFragmentAsync — recall path)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs (v1 contract — MemoryScope/MemoryOrigin — bind CRUD consumers here)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (add/update unit tests — NFR-08)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-042" scope="the Preference fact type and memory write path">Preserve the deferred hard-governance (untrusted-origin ban, trustLevel enforcement, memory-poisoning evals) deferred to security project #616 — `trustLevel` stays carried INERT; do NOT implement or claim those enforcement behaviors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013" scope="Services/Ai/Memory placement and CRUD interaction">Bind CRUD-side memory consumers to `PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs` v1; do NOT inject AI-internal types (`MemoryFactType`, store types) into CRUD code. R4 owns the `Services/Ai/Memory` internals directly (redesign-r2 closed) but the facade discipline holds.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the enum + wire map">Add `Preference` as an EXTENSION of the existing 4-member `MemoryFactType` enum + the `MemoryWriteHandler` wire map — reuse-first (§11); do NOT introduce a parallel preference store or a second write path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="every BFF-touching change">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs) — measure and report absolute + delta; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08" scope="the enum + handler change">Add/update unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/.</constraint>
  </constraints>
