  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add a `Preference` member to `MemoryFactType.cs` (~:12–33) alongside the existing Party/KeyDate/PriorAnalysis/KeyFact.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend the `MemoryWriteHandler.cs` wire map (~:97–104) so the wire token (e.g. `preference`) maps to `MemoryFactType.Preference`.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm recall: a User-scope preference item flows through `ResolveUserMemoryFragmentAsync` (~:644) → `ToUserPromptFragmentAsync` and appears in the `userFragment` assembled at `ResolveUserFragmentAsync` (~:553–583); add coverage if the render path needs the new type.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify CRUD-side consumers bind to `PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs` v1 (MemoryScope/MemoryOrigin); do NOT leak AI-internal types into CRUD code.</step>
    <step order="5">Keep `trustLevel` carried INERT — do NOT implement ADR-042's deferred hard-governance (#616).</step>
    <step order="6">Add/extend unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (Preference writes at User scope; wire map maps it; recall includes it; trustLevel inert).</step>
    <step order="7">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute size + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If adding `Preference` cannot be done without touching ADR-042's deferred hard-governance (untrusted-origin ban / trustLevel enforcement / memory-poisoning evals owned by #616), STOP and escalate (ADR-042 boundary) rather than implementing governance R4 does not own.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`MemoryFactType` enum has 4 members (Party/KeyDate/PriorAnalysis/KeyFact) — NO Preference; `MemoryWriteHandler` wire map maps only those four.</existing>
    <extension>Extend the existing enum + wire map with `Preference` — R4-owned (redesign-r2 closed); no new store, no second write path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Standing directives land as generic `KeyFact` — there is no governed preference channel, and FR-09's narrow-allow-list producer has no fact type to gate on.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
